<title>FRANCE: Paris air cargo exports up 0.8pct in March 97.</title>
<headline>Paris air cargo exports up 0.8pct in March 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>March 1997 air cargo exports from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 52,237 tonnes, up 0.8 percent on the same month in 1996, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The ADP's global export traffic in March 1997, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on March 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic			 3,544		down 10.3</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>    European Union		 6,469		  up 13.4</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe		  1,221		  up  6.3</p>
<p>    North Africa		     819		down 17.0</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa	   4,177		  up  7.1</p>
<p>    North America		 14,909		  up  5.7</p>
<p>    French territories	   2,249		down 12.3</p>
<p>    Latin America		  2,803		down  2.7</p>
<p>    Middle East		    5,232		down  3.9</p>
<p>    Far East			10,814		down  2.8</p>
<p>    Total			   52,237		  up  0.8</p>
<p>---Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax-5017</p>
</text>
